Original commit body from 9170e4f46c8b56b1cc6a48510eaf5b1f38c66fe7:

scip/index.py's _KIND_MAP translated SCIP DescriptorKind to Symbol.kind.
Five of its eight values were registered and three were not
(type_parameter, parameter, meta), plus a fourth minted by a
.get(..., "unknown") fallback. Every ADR-0027 consumer that branches on
Symbol.kind had no case for them. The map is a DICT and axis_drift's
collector read only string-literal SETS, so no drift linter could see it.

REACHABILITY FIRST, which the row filed as its first step. Invoked
rust-analyzer on aardvark-dns and counted descriptor kinds out of the
SCIP index: 681 entries, of which 10 are type_parameter. It is NOT dead
vocabulary -- it is filtered before minting on this crate only because
those entries carry no Definition occurrence, so a survey alone would
have shown a clean artifact and hidden the fact.

unknown is unreachable, provably rather than by sampling: DescriptorKind
is a closed Enum, _KIND_MAP is total over it, and every producer in
descriptor.py constructs from the enum.

parameter and type_parameter are now REGISTERED -- both name a
source-language syntactic construct directly, which is what ADR-0027's
axiom asks of a value.

meta maps to "declaration", the registry's declared catch-all. Not
folded into "attribute", which the registry defines as a data member (a
Python class attribute) rather than what SCIP's ":" suffix means; that
would have been a guess dressed as a verdict. A re-evaluation trigger is
written at the mapping.

The unknown fallback is removed. A KeyError on a future ninth member is
louder and more truthful than silently minting a kind nothing describes.

Two gates the dict never had: every mapped value is a registered
Symbol.kind, and the map is total over DescriptorKind. Both carry a
positive control.

docs/schema.json and docs/concept-axes.md regenerated (both embed the
kind registry).

Closes INV-lagot

